  "tourWelcomeTitle": "See what happens on your bus.",
  "tourWelcomeText": "Busclear listens at your KNX IP gateway and shows every telegram: who sends, to which group address, with which value. This introduction walks you through the main places, with the demo house as an example.",
  "tourConnectTitle": "Connect in one step.",
  "tourConnectText": "Search for the gateway or enter its address, then connect. UDP works with every interface; TCP, routing and KNX IP Secure are under connection type. Each site keeps its own installation with gateway, project and settings.",
  "tourChipSearch": "Find gateway",
  "tourChipInstallations": "Installations",
  "tourProjectTitle": "With your ETS project, every value gets a name.",
  "tourProjectText": "Import the .knxproj file, with password too, or a group address CSV. Then you see names, rooms, data types and devices instead of 1/2/3 and raw bytes. For KNX Secure, add the keyring. Everything stays on the device.",
  "tourChipCsv": "Group address CSV",
  "tourChipLocal": "Stays on the device",
  "tourOverviewTitle": "Overview: every address as a card.",
  "tourOverviewText": "Current value, count and a small history, sorted by rooms and functions. The star keeps favourites, the pin moves a section to the top. The bar at the top counts the telegrams of the last 60 seconds, the hour or the day.",
  "tourObjectsTitle": "Objects: what belongs together stays together.",
  "tourObjectsText": "Command and feedback of a light, all values of a room thermostat: in one card. Actuators appear as DIN rail devices with lit channel LEDs.",
  "tourLiveTitle": "Live: every telegram in order.",
  "tourLiveText": "Time, type (write, read, response), sender, destination, name and value. Anything odd is marked, such as a wrong length or an unusual hop count. Pause stops the list without losing anything.",
  "tourFilterTitle": "Filter instead of searching.",
  "tourFilterText": "The field at the top understands names, addresses, devices and times, also combined. Saved filters are behind the bookmark in the field.",
  "tourChipFilterName": "weather",
  "tourChipFilterSender": "from:1.1.10",
  "tourChipFilterTime": "time:14:05-14:10",
  "tourDetailsTitle": "Details: read, write, comment.",
  "tourDetailsText": "A tap on a card or row opens the details: last value, history, sender and linked devices. From there you read the value again, write your own or attach a comment.",
  "tourHealthTitle": "Health: is the installation fine?",
  "tourHealthText": "One button reads all status addresses and checks what is already there: silent devices, wrong data types, odd cycles, repeats and bus quality. Every finding leads to the address or device.",
  "tourChipSilent": "Silent addresses",
  "tourChipTypes": "Data types",
  "tourChipCycles": "Cycles",
  "tourChipBusQuality": "Bus quality",
  "tourRecordTitle": "Record, comment, report.",
  "tourRecordText": "The red dot records, with name and note. Comments stick to telegrams and recordings, with screenshots. “Report a problem” captures when something went wrong and packs everything for your electrician.",
  "tourHistoryTitle": "History over days.",
  "tourHistoryText": "The long-term history keeps whole days, in the add-on and on the KNX box around the clock. You rewind what happened at night, with a timeline per group address and playback at 1 to 60 times the speed.",
  "tourChipTimeline": "Timeline",
  "tourChipPlayback": "Playback 1–60×",
  "tourChartsTitle": "Charts: several values, one time axis.",
  "tourChartsText": "Up to eight addresses together, one axis per unit, switching values as their own rows. Saved charts appear as their own section in the overview.",
  "tourStatsTitle": "Statistics: who talks the most?",
  "tourStatsText": "Busiest addresses and senders, load peaks and a heatmap over days. A tap on a peak or cell filters the monitor to that time.",
  "tourWatchTitle": "Watchers and alarms.",
  "tourWatchText": "A watcher speaks up with a sound as soon as a given address sends or reaches a value. Alarm and fault objects sit at the top of the overview and send notifications if you like.",
  "tourChipSound": "With sound",
  "tourExportTitle": "Export in every format.",
  "tourExportText": "Telegrams as PDF, CSV or for ETS, reports of health and commissioning, and a ZIP with everything. The exports page keeps the latest files per installation.",
  "tourExpertTitle": "One switch, and the workshop is there.",
  "tourExpertText": "Expert mode on the connect screen or at the bottom of the menu turns on the tools for commissioning and troubleshooting, plus port, tunnel address and connection options. Without it the app stays lean; nothing is lost.",
  "tourChipPort": "Port and tunnel address",
  "tourBusmonTitle": "Bus monitor: every frame.",
  "tourBusmonText": "Raw frames with acknowledgements (ACK, NAK, BUSY), repeats and corrupted telegrams, the senders in a column of their own. The interface has to support bus monitor mode for this.",
  "tourChipAck": "ACK · NAK · BUSY",
  "tourChipRepeats": "Repeats",
  "tourTopoTitle": "Topology: lines and couplers.",
  "tourTopoText": "Devices by line, hop count, tunnels and traffic across couplers. A device opens its sheet with channels, push buttons and addresses.",
  "tourMapTitle": "Communication map: who talks to whom.",
  "tourMapText": "For each address, who sends and who receives according to the project. Solid lines were observed, dashed ones are only in the project.",
  "tourCheckTitle": "Project check.",
  "tourCheckText": "Bus traffic against the ETS project: what is missing, what is unknown, what never sends, plus the flags of the objects even without traffic.",
  "tourCommTitle": "Commissioning and diagnostics.",
  "tourCommText": "The checklist reads every status address in turn and ticks off answers; what is left you check on site, and you get a PDF report. Diagnostics finds devices in programming mode, checks addresses and scans lines.",
  "tourChipProgMode": "Programming mode",
  "tourChipLineScan": "Line scan",
  "tourSendTitle": "Send, trigger, replay.",
  "tourSendText": "Send like the ETS group monitor, delayed or cyclic too. Trigger recordings start on a value, a fault or a repeat, with lead time. A recording can be played back onto the bus, after you confirm it explicitly.",
  "tourBoxTitle": "KNX box for the site.",
  "tourBoxText": "A Raspberry Pi that records around the clock and opens its own Wi-Fi. You pair it with the label; the app fetches the history straight from the box. Still a preview.",
  "tourChipWifi": "Own Wi-Fi",
  "tourChipSticker": "Pair with the label",
  "tourMoreTitle": "More with Plus and Pro.",
  "tourMoreText": "Plus keeps the history over days and adds charts, statistics, watchers and export. Pro unlocks expert mode with bus monitor, topology, commissioning and diagnostics. You can try everything in the demo house.",
  "tourMorePlans": "See the plans",
  "tourReadyTitle": "Ready.",
  "tourReadyText": "In the demo house you try everything safely, without an installation. You find the introduction again on the connect screen at any time.",
