  "projectHelpWhatTitle": "What is a .knxproj?",
  "projectHelpWhat": "Your electrician set up the installation with the planning software ETS. The project file (ending .knxproj) holds all the names: which group address switches the kitchen light, which device sits where, what values there are. With it, Busclear shows names instead of numbers.",
  "projectHelpPasswordTitle": "Project password",
  "projectHelpPassword": "The file may be protected with a password. The app asks for it when importing and needs it only to open the file – file and password stay on your device.",
  "projectHelpKeyringTitle": "Keyring (.knxkeys)",
  "projectHelpKeyring": "If your installation uses KNX Secure (IP Secure or Data Secure), there is also a keyring with its own password. Without it the app can't connect to a secure gateway or read encrypted values. Without Secure you don't need it.",
  "projectHelpGetTitle": "How do I get it?",
  "projectHelpGet": "Ask the company that built the installation. Many hand the file over readily, some for a small fee. For the names, a CSV export of the group addresses from ETS is enough too.",
  "projectHelpTemplateTitle": "Sample request to copy",
  "projectHelpTemplate": "Subject: ETS project file for our KNX installation\n\nHello [name],\n\nYou set up the KNX installation at [address]. For maintenance and troubleshooting we would like to keep an overview ourselves. Could you please send us the current ETS project file (.knxproj) with its project password – and, if KNX Secure is used, the keyring (.knxkeys) with its password as well?\n\nA CSV export of the group addresses would already help too. If there are any costs, please let us know beforehand.\n\nThank you and best regards\n[your name]",
  "projectHelpCopy": "Copy text",
  "projectHelpCopied": "Text copied",
  "projectHelpNoneTitle": "Can't get the file?",
  "projectHelpNone": "Then teach the installation yourself: press a button, name it, done. You'll find it in the monitor under “Teach your installation”. A project imported later takes precedence, your names stay for the rest.",
  "projectHelpDisclaimer": "This is not legal advice. Whether and how you get the file depends on your contract with the company.",
