  "termTunnel": "Tunnel",
  "termGroupAddressText": "A group address (e.g. 1/0/1) is like a channel: a button sends “on” to it, and every actuator listening on that channel switches.",
  "termIndividualAddressText": "The individual address (e.g. 1.1.30) is a device's house number – area, line, device – and tells you who sent a telegram.",
  "termStatusText": "A status is the actuator's answer: it tells you whether the light really is on – not just that someone pressed a button.",
  "termDptText": "The datapoint type says how to read the bytes: 1.001 means on/off, 5.001 percent, 9.001 temperature in °C.",
  "termFlagsText": "Flags define what a device object may do: C communicate, R answer reads, W accept writes, T transmit itself, U take over responses.",
  "termLineText": "A line is one run of bus cable with up to 64 devices; line couplers join several lines into an area.",
  "termTunnelText": "A tunnel is a network access to the bus. An IP gateway has only a few, and every app, ETS or visualisation uses one.",
