  "lessonsTool": "Terms, short lessons and a mini quiz",
  "lessonsIntro": "Five short lessons on your own installation – or in the demo house. Tap a term to see it with an example.",
  "lessonsTry": "Try it: {text}",
  "lessonSwitchTitle": "1 · How KNX switches",
  "lessonSwitchText": "A button doesn't know which light it switches. It just sends “on” to a group address. The actuator listening on that address switches – and reports back on a second address what it did.",
  "lessonSwitchTry": "Watch in the live monitor how an “on” is followed by a status.",
  "lessonWhoTitle": "2 · Who is who",
  "lessonWhoText": "Every device has an individual address like 1.1.30: area 1, line 1, device 30. That shows in every telegram who sent it – even without a project.",
  "lessonWhoTry": "Tap a telegram and look at the sender.",
  "lessonValuesTitle": "3 · Reading values",
  "lessonValuesText": "The bus carries only bytes. The datapoint type turns them into “21.5 °C” or “50 %”. Without it the app guesses from the length – 1 bit is usually switching, 2 bytes usually a measurement.",
  "lessonValuesTry": "Look at the temperatures in the overview.",
  "lessonReadTitle": "4 · Questions and answers",
  "lessonReadText": "The app can “read” an address: it asks, and the device with the read flag answers with the current value. If nobody answers, often just that flag is missing.",
  "lessonReadTry": "The health check asks all status addresses.",
  "lessonConnectTitle": "5 · How the app connects",
  "lessonConnectText": "The app talks over the network to an IP gateway sitting on the bus. For that it uses a tunnel; when all are taken, it has to wait until ETS or a visualisation frees one.",
  "lessonConnectTry": "Tap the gateway name at the top.",
